                    \&amp;\stackrel{(f, Id)}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    B \times B
                    }
                    \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#HomotopyFiberCharacterization Fiber-wise characterization
          #FiberwiseCharacterizationInInfinityGrpds.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              In plain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              (i.e. in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              etc.) the following holds:
            %p
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    C &amp;\stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; D
                    }
            %p
              is a homotopy pullback diagram precisely if it induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
              on all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi hfib
                              %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi hfib
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi b
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    hfib_b(f) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; A &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}  &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    hfib_{p(b)}(g) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; C &amp;\stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; D
                    }
            %p
              for all elements
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CPS05"} CPS 05, 5.2
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/192303/381"} MO
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              For the analog of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FiberwiseCharacterizationInInfinityGrpds"}
              to hold in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
              more general than
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
              one would need either “enough
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+elements"} global elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              to detect all homotopy fibers, or else one would need a suitable “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"}> internal
              ” formulation of the statement.
          %p
            On the other hand in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            the statement holds generally:
          #FiberwiseRecognitionInStableCase.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+category"} stable model category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    C &amp;\stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; D
                    }
            %p the following are equivalent
            %ol
              %li
                %p the square is a homotopy pullback square;
              %li
                %p
                  the square is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
                  square;
              %li
                %p
                  the induced morphism on the homotopy fiber over the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
                  0 is a weak equivalence
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi hfib
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi hfib
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        hfib_0(f) \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} hfib_0(g)
                        \\,.
          %p
            A proof in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+categories"} stable model categories
            including the third item is spelled out for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Hovey07"}> Hovey 07, remark 7.1.12
            ). (Beware: this is not in the original volume from 1999, but is in the version “reprinted with corrections” from 2007.) A proof in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} stable (∞,1)-categories
            is in (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"}> Lurie HA, prop. 1.1.3.4 (2) lemma 1.2.4.14
            ).
          %h3#pasting_law Pasting law
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#fiber_sequences Fiber sequences
          %p
